From d1e80a332081e6023de9e2e64f83bdd8a9cabf53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 15:58:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] compression: openh264 behind a feature

openh264-sys2 builds a C++ decoder from vendored source, which is a
toolchain a pure-Rust consumer does not otherwise need and a second
decoder on a platform that has one in hardware. Off, a STREAM_CREATE
naming H.264 is an unsupported codec like any other.

